{% doc %}
  One product card for the product-page shelves — "You may also like"
  (sv-recommendations) and "Recently viewed" (sv-recently-viewed, which
  builds the same markup in script from /products/{handle}.js, so the two
  shelves are indistinguishable).

  A product still waiting on photography shows sv-system §06's
  placeholder field in the frame rather than a broken image.

  @param {object} product

  @example
  {% render 'sv-card', product: product %}

  Styles live in assets/sv-product.css §20, not a {% stylesheet %} here:
  the storefront bundles a snippet's stylesheet only when the snippet
  RENDERS, and the Recently viewed shelf builds its cards in script.
{% enddoc %}

{%- comment -%}
  The card carries the facts the shelf ranks on — the size run it is made
  in, which of those sizes can actually be bought today, its type and its
  tags. Rendered here rather than fetched again in script: the shelf
  already has the product in hand, and a second request per card to learn
  what size it comes in would be a request per card.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign sizes_all = ''
  assign sizes_live = ''
  for v in product.variants
    assign sizes_all = sizes_all | append: v.title | append: '|'
    if v.available
      assign sizes_live = sizes_live | append: v.title | append: '|'
    endif
  endfor
-%}
<li
  class="sv-card"
  data-sv-card
  data-handle="{{ product.handle }}"
  data-type="{{ product.type | escape }}"
  data-tags="{{ product.tags | join: '|' | escape }}"
  data-sizes="{{ sizes_all | escape }}"
  data-sizes-live="{{ sizes_live | escape }}"
  data-price="{{ product.price }}"
>
  <a class="sv-card__link" href="{{ product.url }}">
    <span class="im r-product sv-card__frame">
      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
        {{
          product.featured_image
          | image_url: width: 700
          | image_tag:
            widths: '300, 450, 600, 700',
            sizes: '(max-width: 760px) 70vw, 300px',
            loading: 'lazy',
            alt: product.featured_image.alt | default: product.title | escape
        }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </span>
    <span class="sv-card__name">{{ product.title }}</span>
    <span class="sv-card__price">
      {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
        <s>{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
      {%- endif -%}
      {{ product.price | money }}
    </span>
  </a>
</li>
